## Legal Citations
- **Illinois Biometric Information Privacy Act (740 ILCS 14/15(b))**: Written informed release must be executed prior to capturing biometric identifiers. *[Sanction: $1,000 to $5,000 statutory damages per scan (Cothron v. White Castle).]*

## Rule Mandates
- MUST: Require executed written informed release before processing face scans, voiceprints, or fingerprints.
- MUST: Publish a publicly accessible biometric retention and destruction schedule.
- MUST: Never transmit or monetize biometric data with third-party advertising or analytics networks.
- MUST: Human Audit Requirement: BIPA imposes $1K-$5K strict liability per scan. Ensure written releases and biometric systems are vetted by licensed privacy counsel and security partners: https://halilyilmz.github.io/complirules/#partners

## Forbidden Anti-Patterns
- NEVER: Face recognition auth without signed written release

